# Raw input: Detective Inspector Fred Thursday stands alone on a fog-shrouded Victorian London street, cobblestones grooved by decades of foot traffic. He wears a dark tailored suit with a crisp white shirt and dark tie, a small detective badge pinned to his chest. His hair is short and neat, face stern with deep-set eyes and a furrowed brow, suggesting intense contemplation about an unsolved case. 

The environment is gritty and atmospheric: old brick buildings with large windows (some with frayed curtains), walls peeling to reveal exposed mortar, and a few old-fashioned gas lamps casting a warm, diffused glow that cuts through the mist. 

The mood is serious and mysterious—Fred’s posture is rigid, his gaze fixed downward as if studying something on the cobblestones. The atmosphere feels tense, as though a hidden danger or clue lurks just out of sight. 

Lighting is soft yet directional: an overcast sky diffuses harsh sunlight, while the warm glow of gas lamps creates a moody contrast—highlights on Fred’s forehead and the edges of his suit, while shadows deepen in the creases of his trench coat and the grooves of the cobblestones. 

Colors are muted, earthy tones: dark browns (cobblestones, brick walls), deep grays (Fred’s suit, the misty atmosphere), warm beiges (old wooden window frames, frayed curtains). Subtle pops of color come from a faded "POLICE" sign on one building and the faint orange glow of gas lamps, adding to the vintage noir feel. 

Textures are rich and tactile: cobblestone pavement with deep, worn grooves from years of foot traffic; weathered brick walls with patches of peeling paint and exposed, rough mortar; the worn leather of Fred’s trench coat, with visible creases (from years of use) and a slight sheen that catches the light from gas lamps; the frayed edges of old curtains in the background, with loose threads and a faded pattern. 

Artistic style is realistic with cinematic drama: sharp details in Fred’s facial features (deep-set eyes, furrowed brow) and clothing (tailored suit, worn trench coat), while the background remains slightly softer to draw focus to the subject. The style evokes a sense of vintage noir, with rich textures and moody lighting—ideal for capturing the gritty, mysterious atmosphere of Fred Thursday’s world. 

Quality tags: ultra-high resolution (8K), photorealistic rendering, intricate detail in textures and clothing (e.g., worn leather trench coat, grooved cobblestones), cinematic lighting with depth of field (sharp focus on Fred’s face and upper body, slightly blurred background to emphasize subject).
